cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this conformance suite in your work, please cite the version you ran, as below, together with the digest of the specification it graded against."
type: software
title: "arcs-conformance: a conformance suite for the Agent Run Conformance Specification (ARCS-1)"
abstract: >-
  A conformance suite for the Agent Run Conformance Specification
  (ARCS-1), the aerospace profile of TRACE (Trust, Runtime Attestation and
  Compliance Evidence), and the public specification of how a conformance
  record in claim@1,
  the conformance claim format, version 1, is serialised, identified, signed
  with Ed25519 (one instance of the Edwards-curve Digital Signature
  Algorithm), verified and withdrawn. The suite tests the software that checks such records. It runs
  any implementation, in any language, through a small protocol of one JSON
  (JavaScript Object Notation) request on standard input and one JSON answer
  on standard output, grades every answer against the clause of ARCS-1 it
  rests on, and reports every case and every one of the specification's
  conformance criteria on its own. It reads the specification from a copy
  checked against the published checksums, builds every artefact from the
  specification's own worked examples, and needs nothing but the Python
  standard library. A pass is evidence about the cases run, not a
  certification. Published and maintained by Ashforde OÜ, a private limited
  company (osaühing) registered in Estonia, under the Apache License,
  Version 2.0 (Apache-2.0); the specification, whose canonical copy is
  published in this repository, keeps its own terms.
